  ],
  "excerpt": "[docs/smtp/README.md#dns-records-at-your-domain-provider]\n- Most providers want only the part before your root domain in *Name*: `mail.inbound` and `inbound` for `example.com`, or `@` for the root domain itself. `10` is the MX priority; some providers have a separate field for it. - **Cloudflare**: set the A record to *DNS only* (grey cloud). The proxy does not carry mail. - Optional, for a subdomain that only receives mail: `TXT inbound \"v=spf1 -all\"`. This says the subdomain never sends mail, so nobody can send spoofed mail from it. - Check the records with `nslookup -type=mx inbound.example.com` and `nslookup mail.inbound.example.com`. Changes show up after a few minutes, sometimes hours.",
